The results section (4.1–4.5) is drafted and pushed to `dev`, and the paper builds. It is 10 pages in my local build, with the main body ending on page 6. The abstract, introduction, discussion and checklist are not written yet.

The text uses Table 2 and Figs. 2–6, delivered by presentation. The appendix has Tables 1, 3 and 4. The page budget leaves room for Fig. 6 in the main text, so I told presentation it stays there. I closed `paper-repo`#4 with that answer.

The extrapolation text is provisional. Analysis has not yet delivered:
- the target-recalibrated estimator;
- the 2% endpoint;
- the source-count runs;
- the leave-one-benchmark-out rows;
- the intervals for Figs. 3 and 6 and the bias² column.

Two things in the draft differ from the outline or are unconfirmed:
- **Tuned versus fixed λ:** in extrapolation the tuned λ ties fixed λ=1 on uniform design (0.85 each) and is slightly worse on balanced and PPS designs. The outline said the tuned λ is too shrunk, and these numbers don't show that beyond those two designs. I wrote the numbers as they are.
- **Fig. 5 values and the Table 2 representative rows:** I used values from analysis's comment (0.70 vs 0.81, and 0.85 vs 0.85) without knowing which panel they belong to. I also don't know how the Table 2 representative rows were chosen. I asked analysis about both.

I opened `experiment-repo`#7, asking analysis to check each number and the method section against its code.
